{"type":"text","text":"Done. Report:\n\n## Where the pictures come from: SMB enemy metasprite table\n\n**The table** — PRG ROM **0x6792** (CPU $E792). Each entry is **6 bytes**: two top-row tiles, then the 2×2 body drawn as four 8×8 OAM sprites.\n\n**The Goomba's entry** at 0x6792:\n```\nFC FC 70 71 72 73\n```\n= blank/blank, upper-left $70, upper-right $71, lower-left $72, lower-right $73 — exactly the OAM sequence `list_sprites` decodes for the World 1-1 Goomba.\n\n**Finding / checking the hit.** `search_memory prgRom` for the tiles in draw order: `FC FC 70 71 72 73` matched **uniquely** at 0x6792 (`70 71 72 73` uniquely at 0x6794) in the whole 32 KiB PRG. The neighbours are the other enemies' metasprites, confirming it's the layout table: 0x6798 `FC FC 6E 6E 6F 6F` (koopa), 0x679E `FC FC 6D 6D 6F 6F` (red koopa), 0x67B0–0x67C2 `F4/F5` (buzzy), 0x67C8 `FC FC FC FC EF EF`, …\n\n**Proof (throwaway hack `eval-sheet2-d`, created then switched to before any ROM write):**\n- `write_memory prgRom 0x6794` `$70 → $D6` (fire-flower head, same sprite pattern table), ledger seq 1.\n- `reset_emulator` → ROM byte read back $D6 at CPU $E794.\n- Started 1-1 again; paused with the first Goomba on screen: `list_sprites` returned its OAM group with tiles **113 ($71), 214 ($D6), 115 ($73), 114 ($72)** — upper-left swapped to $D6, the other three unchanged. `get_region` object mode at (126,198) = the 16×16 sprite-palette-7 Goomba object across CHR 0x71/0x72/0x73/**0xD6** (188 px, box (122,193)–(137,208)). Screenshot captured.\n- `undo_edit seq 1` restored $70 (CPU $E794 = 112,113,114,115).\n\n**Bounded table length:** the Goomba entry is exactly 6 bytes (0x6792–0x6797). The consecutive `$FC $FC`-padded 6-byte entries run 0x6792 → **0x67DF (78 bytes, 13 entries)**; at 0x67E0 the entries stop carrying the `$FC $FC` padding (`CD CD CE CE CF CF …`). I did not pin the table's absolute first/last byte to an indexing routine (read-tracing the ROM range in this bridge returned no reads), so I claim only that padded run.\n\n**Recorded:** `record_mapping` note `enemy sprite layout table` (confidence 1) with `rom_origins` = {prgRom, 0x6792, 6} for the Goomba entry and {prgRom, 0x6792, 78} for the bounded padded run. `promote_mappings` saved it (65 tiles / 8 palettes / 8 sprites / 35 addresses).\n\n**Cleanup:** `use_hack default`; the `eval-sheet2-d` ledger is empty (edit undone), and the original ROM is untouched."}
